  explanation: "For rand_xoshiro 0.8.1, the unchanged native word-generating method of each of its fifteen generators returns Ok of the specified output scrambler and performs the exact documented word-state transition. Coverage includes SplitMix64, both xoroshiro64 variants, all three xoroshiro128 variants, and all three variants of each xoshiro128, xoshiro256 and xoshiro512 family. For 32-bit-word engines the native method is try_next_u32; for 64-bit-word engines it is try_next_u64. SplitMix64::try_next_u32 is also proved independently, including its distinct Mix4 output formula, among the direct body proofs. Each theorem covers arbitrary internal words, including all-zero states, and establishes normal termination in the Aeneas model. Array-state representation theorems establish that the four-word and eight-word inputs cover every valid fixed-length engine state. Exact output formulas and resulting fields are defined independently of the generated Rust body in the output*/next* specifications. The selected original bodies have byte-identical official Aeneas translations under the default and serde feature configurations, so these body guarantees apply to both configurations; this does not verify the serde trait implementations. Nine further 32-bit APIs are verified through exact forwarding selectors whose calls to the unchanged original API are inlined by the Rust compiler: all three xoroshiro128, all three xoshiro256 and all three xoshiro512 variants. These establish the same state transition as their 64-bit method, with low 32 output bits for xoroshiro128++ and xoroshiro128**, and high 32 bits for the other seven variants. The selector source, typed receiver/return correspondence, target, original method inline scopes and absence of unknown externals are guarded. Default and serde selected programs are byte-identical. Four additional direct body proofs cover Seed512: Default initializes all 64 bytes to zero; AsRef exposes exactly the stored bytes; AsMut exposes those bytes and writes back every legal 64-byte replacement unchanged; iter initializes the standard slice-iterator model over those same bytes at position zero. SplitMix64::state is additionally proved to return exactly the eight little-endian bytes of its complete internal u64 state, for every state including zero. All fifteen generators’ state methods are now covered: each returns the complete fixed-length little-endian bytes of every stored unsigned word in field order, for arbitrary internal word patterns including all-zero. Fourteen additional serializers bring the registered total to forty-four: thirty-five direct original bodies and nine compiler-inlined calls. The eight-word serializers also have a decreasing-measure proof that the original enumerate loop terminates after visiting each word. These are serialization results, not serde trait implementation proofs. Independent original-source Kani evidence additionally checks all fifteen from_seed APIs over their full fixed-size byte-seed domains, including the all-zero fallback, and all fifteen state serializers over every valid internal word pattern, including states that seeds may not reach. Default and serde configurations each pass fifteen seed harnesses/6014 checks and fifteen state harnesses/8024 checks. Five separate composition harnesses per configuration (892 checks) cover the remaining 32-bit-engine try_next_u64 operations against independent two-step little-endian output/poststate formulas. These ordinary Kani harnesses are separate tool guarantees, not extra Aeneas machine claims or a mechanized cross-tool equivalence; overlapping serializers are not counted twice. Read-only observers occur only as exact suffixes in generated measurement copies, with original production bytes preserved." -> "For rand_xoshiro 0.8.1 on x86_64 with default or serde features, 69 scoped contracts specify exact outputs and state updates for every internal word pattern, including zero states. Thirty-five direct original-body contracts cover native outputs, all fifteen little-endian state serializers, and Seed512 zero initialization, byte views, legal fixed-length mutable writeback and iterator initialization. Nine compiler-inlined original calls cover 64-to-32-bit projections: xoroshiro128++ and xoroshiro128** use low output bits; the other seven use high bits. Twenty-five further compiler-inlined calls cover the external rand_core 0.10.1 blanket Rng::next_u32/next_u64 specializations, preserving the exact original forwarding behavior and full resulting state. These are external trait specializations, not local declarations. The original selected translations agree under default and serde features; serde implementations themselves are not proved. Eleven two/four-word serializers use the explicitly bounded U32/U64 primitive layout dictionaries; three eight-word serializers prove termination of the original serialization loop. Separate Kani seed/state/composition results remain supplementary evidence, not additional Aeneas claims."
